# Keep the build context to source and manifests.
#
# Without this the context is the whole working tree, and `COPY packages/`
# overwrites the Linux dependencies pnpm just installed with the host's —
# Windows binaries and all. The symptom is `prisma generate` failing on
# "Cannot find module /repo/packages/db/node_modules/prisma/build/index.js",
# which reads like a broken install rather than a stowaway from the host.
#
# A platform that builds from a git archive never sees this, so it fails only
# for whoever runs the command printed at the top of the Dockerfile.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Never in an image, and no reason to upload them either.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Not part of the worker.
apps/web
packages/ui
docs
*.md
!README.md

coverage
**/coverage
